  description: The Moon is Earth's natural satellite and the fifth-largest moon in
    the Solar System. Its surface is covered with craters, mountains, and broad plains
    formed by ancient impacts and volcanic activity, and its gravity influences Earth's
    ocean tides.
  interestingFact: The Moon is tidally locked to Earth, so it takes approximately
    the same amount of time to rotate once as it takes to orbit Earth.
  objectType: 1
